               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_why",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "<p><h3>Why play?</h3>The need to count is not recent. It has existed for a very long time, since before cities or houses existed. We know this because scientists discovered bones with marks in different places (<htcite0> ; <htcite1> ; <htcite2>):</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "a4f22e25-5839-407f-a1aa-634521d52b42",
                     "text": "González Redondo, Francisco A., et al.",
                     "page": "pp. 174 - 177, 180 - 182",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2010",
                        "month": "06",
                        "day": "12"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "ceffba8a-43be-4de3-a5c8-27cdf81311b1",
                     "text": "Puente, Francisco Barriga",
                     "page": "pp. 21 - 23",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2020",
                        "month": "07",
                        "day": "25"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "cd61bc64-1358-4bfd-b343-3629facaa3b4",
                     "text": "González Redondo, Francisco A.",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2024",
                        "month": "10",
                        "day": "27"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": [
                  {
                     "type": "gregory",
                     "year": "2010",
                     "month": "-1",
                     "day": "-1"
                  },
                  {
                     "type": "gregory",
                     "year": "2020",
                     "month": "-1",
                     "day": "-1"
                  },
                  {
                     "type": "gregory",
                     "year": "2024",
                     "month": "-1",
                     "day": "-1"
                  }
               ],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><img id=\"imgBone\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgBone', '0%')\" class=\"imgcenter\"/><b>Figure 1</b>: Representation of a baboon bone with markings. Image by Enrique Silván Pobes, from the work of Francisco A. González Redondo et al.<br />The original is available on ResearchNet (<htcite0>), included here with the authorization of Doctor Francisco A. González Redondo.</p><p>Look at the marks on the bone. They resemble our fingers. In this game, you do the opposite: you look at hands with raised fingers and place marks on a bone until they match.</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "adaed4fb-9c50-4ef9-ab79-c65f3c0629b8",
                     "text": "González Redondo, Francisco A., et al.",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2010",
                        "month": "02",
                        "day": "01"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": [
                  {
                     "type": "gregory",
                     "year": "2010",
                     "month": "-1",
                     "day": "-1"
                  }
               ],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_levels",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "<p><h3>The stages</h3>The game has four stages. In each stage, hands show a number by raising fingers, and you place the same number of marks on the bone:</p><p>In the first stage, you raise fingers of your left hand.</p><p>In the second stage, you raise fingers of your left hand and then of your right hand.</p><p>In the third stage, you and a friend help each other: you raise the fingers of both your hands and also of your friend's left hand.</p><p>In the fourth stage, both people raise the fingers of all their hands.</p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_game",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "<p><h3>Objective and rules</h3><p>Choose which hands will raise fingers using the buttons above the table. Look at the raised fingers. Then use the arrows on the side of the bone to place marks. The up arrow <i class=\"fa-solid fa-caret-up\" style=\"color:#2e7d32;\"></i> adds a mark, and the down arrow <i class=\"fa-solid fa-caret-down\" style=\"color:#1565c0;\"></i> removes a mark. The game stops as soon as the bone shows the same number of marks as raised fingers.</p><p>To keep practicing, start a new round or choose a different set of hands.</p></p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><div class=\"htBoneWrap\"><div class=\"htBoneLevels\" id=\"htBoneLevelsBar\"><span class=\"htBoneLevelsLabel\" id=\"htBoneLevelsLabel\">Hands:</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"yupana-btn htBoneLevelBtn active\" data-level=\"1\">Left hand</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"yupana-btn htBoneLevelBtn\" data-level=\"2\">Left and right hands</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"yupana-btn htBoneLevelBtn\" data-level=\"3\">Both hands and a friend's left hand</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"yupana-btn htBoneLevelBtn\" data-level=\"4\">Both people's hands</button></div><p class=\"htBonePrompt\" id=\"htBonePrompt\">Count the raised fingers, then place the same quantity of marks on the bone.</p><table class=\"htBoneTable\"><thead><tr><th>Raised fingers</th><th>The bone</th><th>Arrows</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class=\"htBoneHandsCell\"><div class=\"htBoneHands\" id=\"htBoneHands\"></div></td><td class=\"htBoneBoneCell\"><div class=\"htBone\" id=\"htBone\"><span id=\"htBoneMarks\"></span></div></td><td class=\"htBoneArrowCell\"><div class=\"htBoneArrows\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-caret-up htBoneArrow htBoneArrowUp\" id=\"htBoneAdd\" role=\"button\" aria-label=\"Add one mark\"></i><i class=\"fa-solid fa-caret-down htBoneArrow htBoneArrowDown\" id=\"htBoneRemove\" role=\"button\" aria-label=\"Remove one mark\"></i></div></td></tr></tbody></table><p id=\"htBoneCongrats\" class=\"htBoneCongrats\" style=\"display: none;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-medal\" style=\"color: gold;\"></i> Congratulations! The marks on the bone match the raised fingers! <i class=\"fa-solid fa-medal\" style=\"color: gold;\"></i></p><p><button type=\"button\" id=\"htBoneNewNumber\" class=\"reset-tutor-btn\">New round</button></p><p class=\"desc\">The arrows beside the bone add or remove marks.</p><span id=\"htBoneHandAltTpl\" class=\"text-store\">Hand with {n} raised fingers</span></div></p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><h3>What are we practicing?</h3>With this game, you practice converting a quantity into a sequence of marks, just as some ancient peoples did on bones. You also practice counting with the fingers of your hands and, when the quantity grows, with the hands of another person.</p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      }
   ],
